# Copy this file to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in your Supabase project's
# values - Settings -> API Keys in the dashboard. Both are required at build/dev
# time; src/supabase/client.ts throws a clear error on startup if either is missing.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is the publishable key (format `sb_publishable_...`;
# Supabase's current replacement for the legacy JWT "anon" key - a legacy anon key
# still works here too, since createClient() accepts either). It is low-privilege
# and safe to ship in the client bundle: see
# docs/adr/0001-host-epoch-and-rpc-only-access.md for why the schema is designed so
# that key alone can't list or tamper with Rooms. Never put a secret key
# (`sb_secret_...`, ex-"service_role") in a Vite env var - anything prefixed
# VITE_ is bundled into the client and shipped to every browser.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key-here
